Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Infra Fiber Bundles", "GuideTitle",
 CellID->942062912,ExpressionUUID->"a3a3c038-ca24-47b7-9945-83f1c1312fe3"],

Cell["\<\
A fibered graph is a graph with a projection onto a base graph, the preimage \
of each base vertex its fiber. It is a fiber bundle when the fibers are \
isomorphic and the edges over each base edge lift consistently. A connection \
chooses how an edge of the base lifts to the fibers; transport along a closed \
walk of the base returns a permutation of the fiber, its holonomy, and the \
connection is flat when every holonomy is trivial. A section picks a vertex \
of each fiber. The Levi-Civita connection is the connection of the tangent \
spaces that the metric singles out. The basic symbols of this layer exist in \
the InfraGaugeTheory paclet and are to be copied here, so every section of \
this guide still waits.\
\>", "GuideAbstract",
 CellID->2001916300,ExpressionUUID->"ef0ab37b-2e0d-4399-8f7e-82603ccbe925"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["", "GuideFunctionsSection",
 CellID->1866139230,ExpressionUUID->"a0ea3657-4c83-4862-93c8-ecf80cebc774"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Fibered graphs", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"56a94ed8-f6df-4532-a7ab-52c3c492402e"],

Cell["\<\
waits: fibered graphs and the bundle conditions, copied from \
InfraGaugeTheory, where they are RandomFiberedGraph, ReconstructBaseGraph, \
IsomorphicFibersQ, EdgeLiftingPropertyQ, LocallyTrivialQ and FiberBundleQ\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"973354c7-045e-4879-acea-9254c558f89e"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Connections and holonomy", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"beb3fc33-f5e0-403e-a40d-8c1fc2a7e2a7"],

Cell["\<\
waits: connections and their holonomy, copied from InfraGaugeTheory, where \
they are ConnectionQ, RandomConnection, ParallelTransport, HolonomyMatrix and \
FlatConnectionQ\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"6728718e-fb45-4656-87bb-2450ff2cf601"],

Cell["\<\
waits: the Levi-Civita connection on the tangent spaces, copied from \
InfraGaugeTheory, where it is FindInfraLeviCivitaConnection with \
InfraParallelTransport, InfraHolonomy and InfraConnectionCurvature\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"fe809cdc-6e58-4bd0-8c4d-aacef08d99a5"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Sections", "GuideFunctionsSubsection",ExpressionUUID->"35a9b48a-ab9a-48e6-9f2d-ca7d37e42da4"],

Cell["\<\
waits: sections of a fibered graph, copied from InfraGaugeTheory, where they \
are RandomSection, SmoothSectionQ and FindZeroSection\
\>", "GuideText",ExpressionUUID->"9b1517c1-3690-49c5-a7aa-1523a5adc34f"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

